 "note_en": "In 世界的末日会以一场大战争的形式到来 \"the end of the world will come in the form of a great war,\" 会 doesn't mean \"can\" but predicts the future, like \"will.\" The whole myth is told with 会: 大地会沉入海中 \"the earth will sink into the sea.\" Since Chinese verbs have no future tense, 会 does the job of English \"will.\"",
